#metadata(title = "PDF Header Footer Review", author = "Mote")
#document(
  default_font = "body",
  default_size = pt(11),
  page = { size = "letter" },
  margin = { top = pt(60), right = pt(60), bottom = pt(60), left = pt(60), header = pt(28), footer = pt(30) }
)
#font(name = "body", latin = "Helvetica")

#header(height = pt(20), distance = pt(18))[
  Mote Header Footer Review #tab() Page #page_number() of #page_number(kind = "total")
]
#footer(height = pt(18), distance = pt(18))[
  Default footer #tab() Confidential
]

# Header And Footer Defaults

The first page uses document-level header and footer defaults. The right side of the header should show the current page and total page count.

| Area | Expected Result |
| --- | --- |
| Header left | Mote Header Footer Review |
| Header right | Page number and total |
| Footer left | Default footer |
| Footer right | Confidential |

#break()

## Second Page With Same Defaults

This page is intentionally created with a page break. It should keep the same top-level header and footer.

- Page numbers should advance.
- The footer should remain stable.
- Ordinary markdown should still render normally.

#section(properties = { start = "next_page" })[
  #header(height = pt(20), distance = pt(18))[
    Section Header #tab() Page #page_number()
  ]
  #footer(height = pt(18), distance = pt(18))[
    Section footer override
  ]

  ## Section-Local Header And Footer

  This explicit section has its own header and footer. It should not affect earlier pages. Future implicit sections should continue to use document defaults unless another section override is declared.

  #table(alignment = "center", cell = { margin = { top = pt(4), right = pt(6), bottom = pt(4), left = pt(6) } })[
    #row[
      #cell(fill = "#e8eef7")[Scope]
      #cell(fill = "#e8eef7")[Header]
      #cell(fill = "#e8eef7")[Footer]
    ]
    #row[
      #cell[Document default]
      #cell[Mote Header Footer Review]
      #cell[Default footer]
    ]
    #row[
      #cell[Explicit section]
      #cell[Section Header]
      #cell[Section footer override]
    ]
  ]
]
